// Provisional allocation-provider seam (contract only).
//
// This trait does not define an Arena language capability or bless bump, slab,
// pool, buddy, or heap semantics. Allocation strategies are ordinary packages
// over qualified `Extent`, placement, and conservation. The current name and
// allocate/deallocate pair predate that reduction and should be judged with the
// future reusable-allocator/container customer rather than treated as settled
// core API.
//
// The concrete range authority returned here is `Extent`; returning a bare
// `addr` would confuse a forgeable number with authority over storage. Reaching
// this boundary requests fresh backing and therefore contributes provider
// reach. Operating on storage already owned by a package does not.
//
// `size`/`align` are byte COUNTS (u64). The returned Extent carries its selected
// geometry in ordinary fields and its grant metadata in domain evidence;
// reclaiming consumes that exact qualified authority.

use omega::language::core::extent;

boundary trait Arena {
    machine allocate(size: u64, align: u64) -> Extent
    reaches
        Arena;

    machine deallocate(extent: Extent)
    reaches
        Arena;
}
